Fix: IBTK::IndexUtilities::mapIndexToInteger() now returns -1 for an index outside
the supplied array extent after periodic adjustment, instead of an integer that
need not correspond to any entry of the array. The three-dimensional
side-centered linear prolongation matrix from
IBTK::PETScMatUtilities::constructProlongationOp() no longer adds a corner
weight that falls outside the physical domain to the wrong neighboring cell.
